From: NixOS Android devices contributors <nixos-android-devices@localhost>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:02:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: acm: stop requeueing failed RX requests

Local fix against U-Boot a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5.
https://source.denx.de/u-boot/u-boot/-/blob/a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c

DWC3 disables an endpoint by giving back pending requests with -ESHUTDOWN
until its request lists are empty. Unconditionally requeueing in the ACM
completion callback prevents this loop from draining when the console is
stopped. Return on a failed completion before copying or requeueing.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
@@ -293,6 +293,10 @@
 {
 	struct f_acm *f_acm = req->context;
 
+	/* Endpoint teardown must drain requests, not queue them again. */
+	if (req->status)
+		return;
+
 	buf_push(&f_acm->rx_buf, req->buf, req->actual);
 
 	/* Queue RX req again */
